jobs.description:
Why Choose TD SYNNEX:

As a Fortune 500 global corporation , operating in over 100 countries, TD SYNNEX values its diverse workforce of 24,000 employees. As the biggest IT distributor in the world, our mission is to provide top-notch technology solutions, empowering businesses and individuals to navigate the digital world safely and efficiently.

Job Purpose:

To build excellent trading relationships with all vendors and internal stakeholders, to obtain competitive advantage for TD SYNNEX, through professional inventory management.

Responsibilities:
- To ensure that maximum stock availability is achieved, through weekly purchasing, to support customer demand, while keeping within inventory budgets;

- To provide management & internal stakeholders with weekly forecasts, to include month–end closing views on inventory & associated costs;

- Monitor sales against forecasts and take appropriate action to maintain stock holding/profile within set budgets;

- Maintain vendor purchase price lists within SAP and ensure inventory held is accurately valued;

- To provide accurate weekly financial reconciliations (e.g. price changes, inventory depreciation);

- To understand and work within all stock related clauses of vendor contracts;

- Develop and review quarterly business plans by vendor with the Business Manager (BM) initiating vendor support as necessary to maintain optimum stock profiles;

- To work closely with BM’s and vendors towards agreed goals and objectives, through proactive inventory management, whilst limiting stock risk through extended negotiated terms and conditions;

- To identify problem stock areas, to review, monitor and implement corrective and preventative actions to conclusion. The key driver is to resolve with minimal cost or lost opportunity to TD SYNNEX;

- To supervise and develop IPP Coordinators;

- To consistently achieve set targets and objectives;

- To work within set policies and procedures and to continually review and update where necessary;

- To own and manage through until completion, any ad hoc projects as defined by IPP Management and escalate as necessary;

- Represent TD SYNNEX at all times in an efficient and professional manner.

Knowledge Skills and Experience
- Strong relationship management;

- Effective communication skills with ability to deliver at all levels;

- Strong negotiation skills;

- Proven experience in inventory forecasting and business planning;

- Must be proactive and self-motivated;

- Must have strong organisation skills with ability to plan, prioritise and maintain focus;

- An enthusiastic team player with a strong drive to create a positive work environment;

- Strong attention to detail;

- Able to work and achieve deadlines under pressure in fast changing environment

- Good working knowledge of MS Office tools (Outlook, Excel) and inventory replenishment systems (SAP R3) would be advantageous;

- Knowledge of Purchasing, inventory principles and practices (CIPS qualified desirable).

What We Offer:

We provide competitive compensation with regular annual salary reviews.
Hybrid work - (3 days at the office, 2 days at home)
We value continuous learning and provide a clear progression plan.
We provide comprehensive benefits including health insurance , paid leave, retirement plans, and more.

